# ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English

Use this standard for docs, code comments, commit messages, PR descriptions, reports, and technical replies.

Keep `public/llms.txt` and on-site copy in Brazilian Portuguese.

## Rules

- Use approved words. Give each word one meaning.
- Use one word for one idea. Do not use two words for the same idea.
- Write short sentences. Keep instructions to 20 words or fewer.
- Use active voice. Write "Turn the switch," not "The switch must be turned."
- Write short paragraphs. Cover one topic in each paragraph.

## Do

```text
Copy `.env.example` to `.env`.
Set the same keys in the Vercel project.
Do not put secrets in `VITE_*` variables.
```

## Do not

```text
Please ensure credentials are configured prior to utilizing the catalog.
The switch must be turned / secrets should never be exposed.
```
